# pkg/salt_plume -- Arctic brine rejection.
#
# Copied 2026-10-02 from
#   ecco_darwin/regions/mac_delta/llc270/biogeochem_setup/AO_ecosystem/
#     setup_files_v0/input/data.salt_plume
# (byte-identical to the llc4320 AO_ecosystem variant -- both carry only
# SPsalFRAC, no file references and nothing grid-dependent, which is why
# this one of the four missing namelists was safe to carry across and
# data.ctrl was not).
#
# SPsalFRAC is the fraction of the salt by-product of seaice GROWTH (not
# melt) redistributed vertically by salt_plume_frac.F; pkg default is 1.0
# (100% effect), range [0,1].
#
# Checked against this build rather than assumed: SALT_PLUME.h declares
# SPsalFRAC as SPsalFRAC(2) only under SALT_PLUME_SPLIT_BASIN, and
# darwin3_ckpt69k/pkg/salt_plume/SALT_PLUME_OPTIONS.h has that #undef
# (as are SALT_PLUME_IN_LEADS and SALT_PLUME_VOLUME). So SPsalFRAC is a
# SCALAR here and the assignment below sets it completely. Under the array
# variant the same line would have set element 1 and silently left element
# 2 at 1.0 -- half the domain at a different brine fraction, with no
# warning. If SALT_PLUME_SPLIT_BASIN is ever defined, this file must
# become two values.
 &SALT_PLUME_PARM01
 SPsalFRAC= 0.5D0,
 &
